{"type":"npc","name":"Storm Conductor","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":115,"temp":0,"max":115,"details":"rejuvenation, void healing"},"ac":{"value":27,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":0,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"fly","value":25}],"details":""},"immunities":[{"type":"bleed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"death-effects","exceptions":[]},{"type":"disease","exceptions":[]},{"type":"paralyzed","exceptions":[]},{"type":"poison","exceptions":[]},{"type":"precision","exceptions":[]},{"type":"unconscious","exceptions":[]}],"weaknesses":[{"type":"sonic","value":10,"exceptions":[]}],"resistances":[{"type":"all-damage","value":10,"exceptions":["force","ghost-touch","sonic","spirit","vitality"],"doubleVs":["non-magical"]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","melodian","necril","voltan"],"details":""},"level":{"value":9},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>A storm conductor forms when the ghost of a conductor who possessed a stormy temperament in life manages to grant their temper an insubstantial spiritual form, causing them to return to life as an unusual form of ghost. A storm conductor wander the land eternally unsatisfied, seeking nothing more than a choir or orchestra that can meet their exacting standards. Sadly, the performers who can do so are few and far between, and so storm conductors are cursed to an eternity of wandering and testing others, and punishing their inevitable failures.</p><p>Turbulent storm clouds swirl in the sky above a storm conductor, providing a constant beat of thunder that, coupled with the eerie orchestral music that surrounds the ghostly creature, makes them rather easy to notice from a significant distance. In combat, the conductor seeks to magically force those they encounter to sing or play along with their invisible orchestra. When one of the conductor's targets fails to meet their expectations, the ghost calls down a violent thunderbolt from the sky above to violently correct their musical inadequacies.</p><h2>Bringing Down the House</h2><p>The stormy weather that whips around a storm conductor prevents the performance of anything but the most bombastic music—a tragedy to those conductors who prefer more delicate, pianissimo works. As one storm conductor bemoaned at the climax of one of her raucous symphonies, \"An eternity of conducting Fanfare of the Storm Giants: a fate worse than Hell itself!\"</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 90/200/360 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> shield, perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Intimidation, Lore [Music], Occultism, Performance)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> charisma, death, dexterity, electricity, energy resistant (acid, cold, electricity, fire, void), intelligence, mind, mind shield, music, sensory (darkvision), spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Ucf8eynbZMfUucjE]{Illusory Scene}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.9AAkVUCwF6WVNNY2]{Lightning Bolt}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.yvs1zN5Pai5U4CJX]{Summon Instrument}, @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.GaRQlC9Yw1BGKHfN]{Wave of Despair}), sturdy, throwing, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"John Willis","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":-5},"dex":{"mod":6},"con":{"mod":0},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":3},"cha":{"mod":6}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":20,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"},{"type":"tremorsense","acuity":"imprecise","range":60}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":15,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":21,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":18,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":19},"intimidation":{"base":19},"occultism":{"base":19},"performance":{"base":21}},"traits":{"value":["ghost","incorporeal","undead"],"rarity":"uncommon","size":{"value":"med"}}},"_id":"rrQWASJf4HM9dxhh","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/storm-conductor.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Storm Conductor","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":1,"height":1,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/storm-conductor.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":2,"scaleY":2,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":2,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/storm-conductor.webp"}},"flags":{"sf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"name":"Music Lore","type":"lore","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"mod":{"value":19},"proficient":{"value":0}},"effects":[],"_id":"9aqVeacK58TC6XVy","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/lore.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"name":"Occult Innate Spells","type":"spellcastingEntry","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"ability":{"value":"cha"},"spelldc":{"value":20,"dc":28},"tradition":{"value":"occult"},"prepared":{"value":"innate"},"showSlotlessLevels":{"value":false},"proficiency":{"value":1},"slots":{"slot0":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot1":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot2":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot3":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot4":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot5":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot6":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot7":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot8":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot9":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot10":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot11":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0}},"autoHeightenLevel":{"value":null}},"_id":"B8bhnzyijDAiM5bV","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/spellcastingEntry.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"folder":"iDjm2cXyRAe4VZ35","img":"icons/environment/wilderness/cave-entrance-vulcano.webp","name":"Illusory Scene","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You craft an imaginary scene that includes up to 10 discrete creatures or objects of various sizes, all of which must be within the spell's area. These elements generate appropriate sounds and smells, and they feel right to the touch. Elements of an illusory scene are incapable of speech. Unlike with the @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.spells.Item.f8SBoXiXQjlCKqly]{Illusory Creature} spell, creatures in your scene lack combat abilities and statistics. Your scene doesn't include changes to the environment around it, though you can place your scene within the illusory environment of a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-anachronism.spells.Item.HBJPsonQnWcC3qdX]{Mirage} spell.</p>\n<p>When you create the scene, you can choose to have it be static or follow a program. Though a static scene is stationary, it includes basic natural movement. For example, wind blowing on an illusory piece of paper would rustle it. A program can be up to 1 minute long and repeats when finished. For instance, you could create a scene of two orcs fighting each other, and the fight would go the same way for each repetition. If you create a loop, the two fighters end up in the same place at the start of the scene and at the end of it, but you can smooth the program so it's hard to tell when the loop ends and begins. Anyone observing the scene for more than a few minutes almost always notices it looping. You're unable to alter the program after you create the illusion.</p>\n<p>Any creature that touches any part of the image or uses the @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.actions.Item.BlAOM2X92SI6HMtJ]{Seek} action to examine it can attempt to disbelieve your illusion. If they interact with a portion of the illusion, they disbelieve only that portion. They disbelieve the entire scene only on a critical success.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (6th)</strong> Creatures or objects in your scene can speak. You must speak the specific lines for each actor when creating your program. The spell disguises your voice for each actor.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (8th)</strong> As the 6th-rank version, and the duration is unlimited.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"illusory-scene","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["auditory","concentrate","illusion","manipulate","olfactory","visual"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","occult"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":5},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":"500 feet"},"area":{"type":"burst","value":30},"time":{"value":"10 minutes"},"duration":{"value":"1 hour","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"B8bhnzyijDAiM5bV","heightenedLevel":5},"counteraction":false},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.sf2e.spells.Item.Ucf8eynbZMfUucjE","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"aLmKzU74xAeUMJmb"},{"folder":"4fJHnYFqH0VjZXPv","img":"icons/magic/lightning/bolt-strike-sparks-blue.webp","name":"Lightning Bolt","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A bolt of lightning strikes outward from your hand, dealing 4d12 electricity damage.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 1d12.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"lightning-bolt","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","electricity","manipulate"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":""},"area":{"type":"line","value":120},"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"","sustained":false},"damage":{"0":{"applyMod":false,"category":null,"formula":"4d12","kinds":["damage"],"materials":[],"type":"electricity"}},"defense":{"save":{"basic":true,"statistic":"reflex"}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"B8bhnzyijDAiM5bV","heightenedLevel":5},"counteraction":false,"heightening":{"damage":{"0":"1d12"},"interval":1,"type":"interval"}},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.sf2e.spells.Item.9AAkVUCwF6WVNNY2","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"oxxoKJTKCqe28Trg"},{"folder":"iDjm2cXyRAe4VZ35","img":"icons/creatures/slimes/slime-face-teeth-purple.webp","name":"Wave of Despair","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>You inflict despair on creatures in the area. The effects for each creature are determined by its Will save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> For 1 round, the creature can't use reactions and must attempt another save at the start of its turn; on a failure, it is @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.xYTAsEpcJE1Ccni3]{Slowed 1} for that turn as it sobs uncontrollably.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> As success, but the duration is 1 minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, and the creature is automatically slowed 1 for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (7th)</strong> The area increases to a 60-foot cone.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"wave-of-despair","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","emotion","manipulate","mental"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","occult"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":5},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":""},"area":{"type":"cone","value":30},"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"1 or more rounds","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":{"save":{"basic":false,"statistic":"will"}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"B8bhnzyijDAiM5bV","heightenedLevel":5},"counteraction":false,"heightening":{"levels":{"7":{"area":{"type":"cone","value":60}}},"type":"fixed"}},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.sf2e.spells.Item.GaRQlC9Yw1BGKHfN","